[{:adr/consequences "{:shared_pipeline \"chart/graph/math/document generation in any kotoba actor can go through a shared, portable, dependency-free EDN pipeline (d3 scale/shape -> svg path strings; katex parse -> MathML; tex AST -> LaTeX source; force3d simulation -> node positions) instead of ad hoc JS interop or bespoke per-project code\", :composability \"kotoba-lang/d3's path-string output and kotoba-lang/katex's MathML output are wire-compatible with kotoba-lang/svg/html's Hiccup-like [:tag {attrs} children] shape without a hard dependency on those repos\", :independent_from_rust_kami_graph \"force3d gives kotoba a JVM/cljs/SCI/GraalVM-portable force-directed layout not requiring the Rust kami-engine toolchain, at the cost of a separate implementation from kami-graph (accepted: different runtime targets and consumers)\", :v1_scope_narrow \"Barnes-Hut/octree optimization (force3d), full TeX math grammar / glyph-level layout (katex), curved-line interpolation and axis rendering (d3), and a TeX engine/compiler (tex) are all explicitly deferred, not blocking this registration\", :deferred_unrelated_wip \"the primary working directory's kami-provider-catalog manifest/repos.edn WIP remains uncommitted and unaffected by this ADR's registration, landed independently via a separate clean worktree\"}", :adr/authoritative_for ["kotoba-lang/tex is an EDN-first LaTeX-source *document generator* (Hiccup-like AST -> string), not a TeX engine/compiler" "kotoba-lang/katex is a native TeX-math-subset parser + EDN AST + MathML renderer, not a JS/npm KaTeX.js interop wrapper and not a full glyph-level font-metric layout engine" "kotoba-lang/force3d is a pure-functional, portable 3D force-directed simulation on plain EDN node/link maps, independent of (not a WASM bridge to) the Rust kami-graph crate in orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine" "kotoba-lang/d3 covers the d3-scale + d3-shape analogue only (scales, line/area/arc generators, pie-layout) -- no DOM selection/data-binding, no transitions, no force layout (that is force3d)" "all four repos are plain nouns with no -clj suffix, zero third-party runtime deps, .cljc, registered under kotoba-lang org via manifest/repos.edn :extra-projects"], :adr/supersedes [], :adr/superseded_by [], :adr/topic "kotoba-lang-viz-typesetting-substrate", :adr/related ["CLAUDE.md" "90-docs/adr/2607011130-kotoba-svg-did-edn-substrate.md" "manifest/repos.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine/CLAUDE.md"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607012000-kotoba-lang-viz-typesetting-substrate", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-01", :adr/decision "{:new_repos [{:path \"orgs/kotoba-lang/tex\", :remote \"kotoba-lang\", :visibility :private, :head_sha \"3491a3a74234b706761d00dfbbdda74e4c447816\", :scope \"EDN Hiccup-like LaTeX document generator: render/escape/raw/command/env primitives; document/section/subsection/subsubsection/itemize/enumerate/item/math/display-math/frac/sqrt/tabular helpers\", :tests \"19 tests / 45 assertions, 0 failures (clojure -M:test)\"} {:path \"orgs/kotoba-lang/katex\", :remote \"kotoba-lang\", :visibility :private, :head_sha \"63ce122a66c0b7b0379c48d0ba086bfd4b1c561a\", :scope \"kotoba.lang.katex.parse: recursive-descent TeX-math-string -> EDN AST (frac, sup/sub/supsub, sqrt/nth-root, greek letters, common operators/relations, grouping, :unknown fallback). kotoba.lang.katex.mathml: AST -> MathML EDN -> XML string\", :tests \"20 tests / 53 assertions, 0 failures (clojure -M:test)\"} {:path \"orgs/kotoba-lang/force3d\", :remote \"kotoba-lang\", :visibility :private, :head_sha \"f1a76c2e227230b2a384c15a06d8990d5ff65ed9\", :scope \"kotoba.lang.force3d.core: simulation state {:nodes :links :forces :alpha ...}; composable forces charge/link/center/collision (all x/y/z, true 3D); simulation/tick/simulate integrator with alpha decay\", :tests \"10 tests / 17 assertions, 0 failures (clojure -M:test); one real charge-force sign-convention bug found and fixed during scaffolding (negative :strength was attractive instead of repulsive)\"} {:path \"orgs/kotoba-lang/d3\", :remote \"kotoba-lang\", :visibility :private, :head_sha \"eed5dd8cc1b5cd8009c3559e776872564c976d30\", :scope \"kotoba.lang.d3.scale: linear-scale/linear-invert, log-scale/log-invert, ordinal-scale, point-scale, band-scale. kotoba.lang.d3.shape: line-generator, area-generator, arc-generator (large-arc-flag + full-circle edge cases handled), pie-layout\", :tests \"17 tests / 52 assertions, 0 failures (clojure -M:test)\"}], :scaffold_method \"four independent general-purpose subagents, one repo each, run in parallel (no shared-file writes -- each confined to its own new repo directory and git history; manifest/repos.edn, manifest/west.yml, and ADR authorship were explicitly withheld from all four and centralized afterward)\", :manifest_registration {:repos_edn \"added the four orgs/kotoba-lang/{tex,katex,force3d,d3} paths to :extra-projects\", :west_yml \"regenerated via nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs inside a fresh git worktree (/tmp/wt-viz-libs) created from origin/main tip (git worktree add -b manifest/register-viz-libs), with the four new repos' working-tree checkouts copied into the worktree's orgs/kotoba-lang/ so working-head could resolve their pins; all other ~450 existing projects' working trees were absent from this worktree by design, so gen-west-manifest.cljs fell back to their existing west.yml-recorded revisions unchanged\", :verify \"a name->revision diff of west.yml before/after regeneration showed added=[d3 force3d katex tex], removed=[], changed-revisions=[] -- confirming the regeneration touched only the four new entries; nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs --check passed (exit 0); pin == child-repo HEAD confirmed for all four (matches the head_sha values above)\", :why_clean_worktree_not_primary_checkout \"the primary superproject working directory had unrelated uncommitted WIP on manifest/repos.edn (kami-provider-catalog split) and a local branch that could not git merge --ff-only origin/main (persistent shallow-graft 'unrelated histories' error despite gh api compare confirming a true fast-forward); a clean worktree off origin/main tip avoided both bundling that WIP and fighting the shallow-merge issue\", :preserved_wip \"the pre-existing manifest/repos.edn WIP in the primary working directory (/Users/junkawasaki/github/com-junkawasaki) was never discarded -- verified via git stash push/pop round-trip, left in place, untouched, for its own owner to land separately\"}}", :db/id -1, :adr/problem "{:source \"owner request 2026-07-01: asked whether d3/force3d/katex/tex were already cljc/kotoba lib-designed under kotoba-lang; answer was no (only orgs/kotoba-lang/kami-engine/kami-graph, a Rust force-directed-layout crate, and .tex paper-source build artifacts existed); owner then said 'ok, do it' and, via clarifying questions, chose: all four libs, native implementation (not JS/npm wrappers), registered as new kotoba-lang repos\", :investigated [\"grep across orgs/kotoba-lang for d3/force3d/katex/tex found no dedicated library -- kami-graph (Rust, inside kami-engine) and main.tex paper sources (LaTeX build artifacts, not a library) were the only hits\" \"kotoba-lang naming convention confirmed via directory listing: svg, did, html, css, rdf, turtle, shacl, ooxml, drawingml, coll, json, spec, wit, async, device -- all plain nouns, no -clj suffix\" \"kotoba-lang/coll (deps.edn/README/src/test shape) and kotoba-lang/svg (Hiccup-like EDN element convention, [:tag {attrs} & children] -> deterministic string render) used as the canonical templates for all four new repos\" \"GitHub name availability confirmed via gh api repos/kotoba-lang/{d3,force3d,katex,tex} (all 404 before creation) and org write access confirmed via gh api orgs/kotoba-lang\"], :risk \"the primary superproject working directory had a large pre-existing uncommitted WIP on manifest/repos.edn (kami-provider-catalog split, ~90 line diff) at session start; a naive local edit + nbb scripts/gen-west-manifest.cljs + commit in that same working tree would have bundled or clobbered that unrelated WIP. Separately, the local branch (codex/ec-maturity-20) was on an old shallow-grafted commit and could not git merge --ff-only origin/main even after git fetch --deepen=30 (persistent 'refusing to merge unrelated histories' from a stale shallow graft boundary), despite gh api compare confirming a pure fast-forward (ahead_by 28, behind_by 0, merge_base == local tip)\"}", :adr/alternatives "[{:option \"JS/npm interop wrappers around real d3.js/KaTeX.js\", :rejected_because \"owner explicitly chose native implementation over interop wrapping, consistent with the zero-third-party-runtime-dep, EDN-first convention already established by svg/html/css/did and the rest of the kotoba-lang substrate family\"} {:option \"bridge force3d to the existing Rust kami-graph crate via a WASM boundary\", :rejected_because \"adds a WASM bridge dependency and couples a portable JVM/cljs library to the game-engine build toolchain; the force-directed-layout algorithm itself is small and well-known enough that a straightforward native reimplementation was simpler and kept the library dependency-free\"} {:option \"attempt full feature parity (complete TeX math engine incl. glyph/font-metric layout, full d3.js module set incl. selections/transitions, a real LaTeX compiler)\", :rejected_because \"each is independently a multi-month undertaking; scoped v1 surfaces (documented per-repo above) ship a solid, well-tested core now, matching how kotoba-lang/coll and kotoba-lang/svg were themselves scoped as focused rather than exhaustive\"} {:option \"regenerate manifest/west.yml directly in the primary superproject working directory\", :rejected_because \"that working directory had unrelated uncommitted WIP on the same file (kami-provider-catalog split) and a local branch stuck behind origin/main by a shallow-graft artifact that git merge --ff-only could not resolve even after git fetch --deepen=30; a clean worktree off origin/main tip avoided bundling the unrelated WIP and avoided fighting the shallow-merge issue entirely\"}]", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607012000: kotoba-lang/{tex,katex,force3d,d3} — visualization/typesetting EDN-first substrate"}]